From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MastaG <mastag@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 15:40:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu/gmc10: BC-250 KFD VMID flushes over MMIO, not the
 KIQ

Without HWS (sched_policy=2) kfd_flush_tlb() flushes a process's static
VMID by number (0025-bc250-kfd-nohws-vmid-flush.patch). That goes through
amdgpu_gmc_flush_gpu_tlb() to gmc_v10_0_flush_gpu_tlb(), which hands it to
the KIQ whenever the KIQ is up -- the route 0006 already takes the GFX1013
PASID flushes off. Under sustained compute from several processes the
KIQ stops answering: "failed to write reg 28b4 wait reg 28c6" and
"Timeout waiting for VM flush hub: 0!", each one stalling its caller for
seconds.

Route GFX hub flushes of KFD VMIDs (first_kfd_vmid and up) on the BC-250
through the same MMIO, semaphore-guarded, type-0 path as the PASID
flushes. Graphics VMIDs and the GART flush (VMID 0) keep their route.
GFXOFF is held off while a KFD process is active (0007), so the MMIO
access is safe there.

Tested on a BC-250 (40 CUs, sched_policy=2, kernel 7.3.1-1.391) with a
HIP stress test that reallocates buffers every iteration under a
continuous ALU load and checks each result on the CPU:
- three processes, 2 min: before, ~20 KIQ flush failures and 3328
  iterations in 135 s; after, none and 5085 iterations in 120 s;
- four processes, 10 min: 40762 iterations, 0 wrong results, no kernel
  messages.
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gmc_v10_0.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gmc_v10_0.c
index 2eb8185b3..97346e210 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gmc_v10_0.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gmc_v10_0.c
@@ -357,8 +357,21 @@ static void gmc_v10_0_flush_gpu_tlb_internal(struct amdgpu_device *adev,
 static void gmc_v10_0_flush_gpu_tlb(struct amdgpu_device *adev, uint32_t vmid,
 					uint32_t vmhub, uint32_t flush_type)
 {
+	/*
+	 * BC-250: a KFD VMID's GFX hub flush must not go through the KIQ
+	 * either. Without HWS, kfd_flush_tlb() flushes the process's static
+	 * VMID by number; under sustained concurrent compute the KIQ then
+	 * stops answering ("failed to write reg ... wait reg ...", several
+	 * seconds each). Take the same MMIO, semaphore-guarded, type-0 path as
+	 * the PASID flushes.
+	 */
+	bool bc250_kfd_vmid = adev->pdev->device == 0x13FE &&
+		amdgpu_ip_version(adev, GC_HWIP, 0) == IP_VERSION(10, 1, 3) &&
+		vmhub == AMDGPU_GFXHUB(0) &&
+		vmid >= adev->vm_manager.first_kfd_vmid;
+
 	gmc_v10_0_flush_gpu_tlb_internal(adev, vmid, vmhub, flush_type,
-					   false);
+					   bc250_kfd_vmid);
 }
 
